sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: swamp-load-git-checkout (Nick 2026-11-01), release-waits-for-swamp, single-swamp-node. docs/reference/gateway-recovery.md#load-swamp.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, Nick approved Gateway grant rendering; official file actions run after checkout and before reload.
  %% Orchestrator 2026-11-08: the load reports collections drift and never installs; the swamp role converge stays the one install path.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: gateway:release:deploy · Load Swamp
  %% kind: gateway.swamp_load
  %% behavior name: gateway-swamp-checkout, gateway-swamp-collections, gateway-swamp-load, release-<gateway|serve>-grants-209 (fixed)
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>release runner
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 209<br/>serve checkout
  Note over GW: Release reaches Load<br/>after migrate, before switch
  %%> When:
  %%> - every Gateway release, automatic or `orbit gateway:release:deploy <sha>`
  %%> - after prepare and migrate, before the switch
  %%> - also for releases that change no Swamp file, so Gateway and Swamp always run the same commit
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no CLI command of its own; the release runner is the only caller
  %%> - `gateway:release:rollback` skips this step, so a rollback works while Swamp is down
  Note over GW: Render target grants<br/>freeze grants and SSH target
  GW->>SW: Start load run<br/>operation-gateway-swamp-load
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - records task #5150 with the release commit
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve, placed on the `swamp` role
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the release commit, for example `a1b2c3d`, its rendered grants and the admitted SSH target
  %%> Retry:
  %%> - when serve is restarting, the start waits up to 10 minutes instead of pausing the release
  SW->>N: checkout<br/>git checkout --detach a1b2c3d
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the new commit descends from the current one (fast-forward only)
  %%> On the Node:
  %%> - fetches the commit into the serve checkout
  %%> - moves the checkout to it
  %%> Why:
  %%> - Swamp's default mode reads `swamp/` from a Git checkout; no custom loader
  SW->>N: grants<br/>cfgmgmt file · two files
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the Gateway-rendered `orbit-gateway.yaml` and `orbit-serve.yaml` under `swamp/grants/`
  %%> - uses the admitted SSH target with owner `orbit`, group `orbit` and mode `0640`
  %%> - the two fixed file behaviors run in parallel; a failed write stops the load
  SW->>N: Check the collections<br/>cmp requirements.yml · pin
  %%> Runs beside the grants: both start after the checkout.
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - compares the commit's `swamp/ansible/requirements.yml` with `/opt/orbit/ansible/requirements.yml`, the pin the swamp role last installed its collections from
  %%> - equal files pass; it installs nothing either way
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a different file fails only this step: the load and the release go on, and the release record shows `phases.swamp.warning` `swamp.collections_drift` with the fix `orbit node:role:add 209 swamp --converge`
  %%> Why:
  %%> - `requirements.yml` changes about once a month; the swamp role converge is the one path that installs collections  alt Load succeeds
    N->>SW: load<br/>swamp serve reload, access reload
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - `swamp serve reload`: serve picks up new and changed workflows and extensions
    %%> - extensions come with their manifest `additionalFiles`, so a newly shipped file needs no serve restart (Lab #4282, fixed in db3f6373)
    %%> - `swamp access reload`: serve creates, revokes or keeps grants to match the file
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a reload, not a restart: running work keeps going
    Note over SW: load checks commit<br/>swamp workflow list
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - compares the workflows serve runs with the workflows in the commit
    %%> - ignores the `schedule-<uuid>` workflows that Schedules publish
    SW-->>GW: Loaded<br/>sha, previous, workflows
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5150 succeeded
    %%> - returns the commit, the previous commit and the workflow count
  else Load fails
    SW--xGW: Load failed<br/>gateway.release_swamp_load_failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5150 failed
    %%> - the release pauses before the switch; the old Gateway release stays live
    %%> - the checkout may stay on the new commit; fix forward and resume the release
  end
  Note over GW: Release goes on<br/>switch, verify
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Gateway and Swamp now run the same commit
  %%> - the release switches to the new Gateway code
